            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral thalamic pain secondary to bilateral thalamic infarcts relieved by a further unilateral ischaemic episode.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>717-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study reports a patient with severe, debilitating bilateral thalamic pain caused by bilateral thalamic infarcts. The authors consider it to be a unique case as a further clinically unilateral lesion led to pain relief bilaterally.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 1999 Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
